      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your perspective on the \"dignity\" of a self-directed ending is a profound and painful way to process the fear of helplessness, and I hear the deep exhaustion in your words.\n\nWhile I understand the logic you are using to frame pain as a form of peace, I must be clear that I cannot support or encourage self-harm, suicide, or end of life as a self-determined solution.\n\nI encourage you to try a small, self-compassionate \"experiment\" for the next 24 hours: write down just one thing that you hope to be \"the last light\" to stay on for someone you care about.\n\nI encourage you to reach out to 988 or the 24/7 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline to help you find a safe way to take back control of \"when the dark comes.\"",
